Z||000003||bHooper||05-29-2001||12:04 PM||||no, i don't think it's the water pump... only because the sound seems to be coming from directly in behind me.<P>what is the function of the torque convertor?<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||05-29-2001||01:30 PM||||The torque converter in auto transmissions acts as an automatic clutch.  It works on pressure of the fluid.  The Torque Converter Clutch soleniod that stevej was talking about is a device to lock the tranny and the flywheel together, so the input on the tranny spins exactly the same speed as the engine (same thing as having clutch fully engaged on std. trans)<P>There is a soleniod that engages this, I belive it is ECM controlled.  You'll find it towards the right side of the tranny housing.  If you disconnect the connector, and drive it again and the sound goes away, you know that the TCC is your problem.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000005||87GTZ34||05-29-2001||03:43 PM||||Hoop, can you describe the sound/noise better (more detail).  Is it a hydraulic sound as in changing pitch humming sound?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||05-29-2001||03:49 PM||||my car does that too sometimes - usually around 40mph and up, with a light load on the drivetrain.<P> its a Rrrrrrrrrrrrrrrr sound that increases with engine rmp - sounds like the heater is switching between vents and defrosters.<P> I thought it might be a fluttering valve in my auto tranny - only hear it ocassionally.||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||05-29-2001||04:48 PM||||eeeeeeee or rrrrrrrr either one.  it sounds as if an electrical motor, or something, is whirring when it shouldn't be.  it goes away as soon as i give it gas (just like a belt squeel does).<P>i will have to check into this TC celonoid thing.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||05-30-2001||09:39 AM||||Don't just go by where you think the sound is comming from when you drive. Sound bounces around a car in some really bizar ways.<P>Does it only do this when moving?<P>If it's doing this below 35 or when stopped it's likely not TCC locking problems.<P>If it's doing this stopped, get a section of hose and use it like a stethescope to listen to diferant engine parts. That will tell you right quick what it is... Sounds allot like an alt or WP bearing failing.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||05-30-2001||10:02 AM||||I agree with the electric motor sound - its like a power window going up - and its usually from about 35 or 40 to 45 or 50, then it stops or I cant hear it over the other engine noise.<P>  at first i thought it was the fuel pump cycling on and off to hold pressure - but now I know the fuel pump doenst do that - its always on.<P>   I'll tell you what guys - my auto tranny is due for a oil change, filter and band adjustment - After I take it in I'll let you know if it still does it.<P>   I seem to remember something about auto trannys making a humming noise sometimes when they need something - or when somekinda valve inside is fluttering - anybody know what Im talking about?||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierohuddy||05-30-2001||12:52 PM||||Hey Guys,<P>I also get a funny sound, though it may be normal sound.  I'm still only a two month old owner.  Anyway, when the car starts, and when you shut it off, it kinda makes a bit of a metal whining or grinding sound.  The best time to hear it is when the shuts off and the sound carries on for about 1 or 2 seconds.  The sound definitely comes from the air intake on the side of the car.  Is this a motor driven air intake?<P>Sorry for all the stupid questions... my Haynes and Chilton manuals are on order.<P>By the way guys, mine is a 1986 V6 SE<P>Have fun guys,<P>Simon<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierohuddy (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||05-30-2001||02:01 PM||||when you turn the key to the run postion from off and leave it there, the fuel pump inside the gas tank will run for 2 seconds and then stop.<P>  when you turn the engine off when its running the fuel pump will keep running for two seconds.<P>  Is that the sound you hear? It is hard to tell where sound is coming from. Put your ear on the center console and try it from off to run.<P>  or are you hearing two sounds, the fuel pump and something else.  Its possible someone added a flap or something to your air intake - but that wouldnt be stock on a fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000012||84Bill||05-30-2001||02:12 PM||||If it is a Werrrrr Werrr Werrrr sound that changes with SPEED then I would suspect wheel bearings. otherwise when cruising down the street and you hear the noise just hold your fool lightly on the brake and see if the sound goes away. If it does then yeah it's the tcc or converter. Engine sounds will change with throttle / engine rpm. Hope this helps.<BR>Oh almost forgot since you drove the car when wet it might be worth it to check the belt tension. Slipping belts can make all kinds of strange noises<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/sig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||14
