Z||000015||SteveJ||05-31-2001||09:49 AM||||I don't know if its slipping or defective but on mine it did start to stay locked up. I was going thru the toll barrier at Pennsylvania when the car stalled at the barrier so it was good and hot. Had to push the car to the side. Waited a few minutes and unplugged it. Continued on my way. Gotta think the sound and subsequent failure are in some way related but I don't know.||||reg||1
Z||000016||87GTZ34||06-01-2001||05:41 PM||||Well, I guess you could eliminate the TCC by disconnecting it at the relay for a spin or two.  As I mentioned in another thread, my alt makes a very high freq sound almost like a turbo.  This is not belt squeal as I have that too and this noise is in addition to the squeal.  This all started after washing the car???<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 06-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||bHooper||06-01-2001||10:37 PM||||My sound definately is a Rrrrr noise and is absolutely coming from the tranny area.  I heard this evening when I cranked the car, and imediately got out and reved the engine at the throttle body (which reproduced the sound)!<P>So, what does all these torque thingys actually do?!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000018||Tweek||06-02-2001||12:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B><BR>So, what does all these torque thingys actually do?!<P>hoop</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When I was younger my dad described a torque converter to me like this:<P>Its kinda like a box with 2 fan blades inside which are realy close together, like right up against each other. Now the box is filled with oil so that when one blade turns, (the one from your motor) it make the other one want to turn, but doesnt force it. Thats why you can have it in drive with the brake on and it doesnt stall, like a standard trans would. <P>A TCC simply locks the blades together at higher speeds to give you better gas milege, less power, but better for your pocket.<P>The tcc is supposed to disengage when you slow down or speed up, when it doesn't disengage and you slow down a lot, you will stall. Like a standard will if you dont press in the clutch, or take it out of gear or downshift or somethin...<P>I hope that kinda help, someone let me know if I am way off.<P>-Ted||||reg||1
Z||000019||Mach10||06-02-2001||05:17 PM||||I'll add to what Ted Sed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .<P>He described it fairly accurately. What it DOES do, also is act as an Infinitley variable gear-ratio. The slower the unit spins, the higher the gear ratio. The faster it spins, the closer the gear ratio. At higher revs, the ratio is almost 1-1. What the TCC actually does is close the ratio up to true (almost. There's ALWAYS slippage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)1-1 at a lower speed. This makes cruising nicer, and allows a sort of "4th" gear (not quite).<P>My car makes a consistant whirring noise. I thought it was from behind, but closer inspection turns out to be one of the int. fans under the dash. It's not a bad noise. ||||reg||6
Z||000020||Ken Wittlief||06-04-2001||09:58 AM||||I was driving my car this weekend and I could swear the Rrrrrrr sound in my car is coming from the front - maybe the vacuum assist on the brakes under the front hood.<P>I do have brake problems - I can get a good pedal with the engine off, and I have bled them to death, but with the engine running I can put the brake pedal right to the floor. The car stops pretty well, but it wont skid the tires. It doenst pump up, the pedal is always the same - it feels like the master cylinder 'gives' when you step on it hard.<P>  I am getting a rebuilt master cylinder today for it, if that doesnt fix it then all that is left is the power boost vaccum assemble.<P>   maybe thats what I hear on mine, maybe the vacuum assembly is fluttering or leaking a little vacuum at just the right engine speed.<P>  that could also explain why touching the brakes makes the sound stop - maybe its not the TCC on my car - will let you know what I learn as I get my brakes up to snuff.||||reg||1
Z||000021||bHooper||06-04-2001||10:38 PM||||ok, Bob Englert and I listened to the sound, with the car in park, neutral and drive, sitting in the driveway today.  It is a definate Rrrrr sound, and is either coming from the Distributor area or the tranny.  I suspect distributor as I witnessed the spartplug wires rotating (while the sound occured) on the coil!<P>Could it be that the distributor is out of whack?  Maybe the rotor is bad?<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000022||87GTZ34||06-05-2001||12:14 AM||||What does the inside of the distributor look like? i.e. is it pretty rusted up?  I was thinking maybe you're getting subtle contact on the pickup due to rust. Also if the bushing is worn, it may have wobble from the shaft.  <P>Use the garden hose/stethoscope trick and that should definitively tell you which of those (if any) is the source.||||reg||1
Z||000023||SteveJ||06-05-2001||08:25 AM||||Making the noise at idle and in park? Absolutly not the TCC and there is not much else that can go wrong with a torque converter in normal use. ( in those 500 and 600 HP engines yea they get problems when they load 'em up for startup ) <BR>Rotating sparkplug wires? Cool I've never seen that. Might be worth the trip to see. Wires so loose they spin probably have a gap inside which makes noise when the spark jumps. Just a thought but maybe you don't want to fix that. Might make a nice side show at the Fiero meets. You could charge to see it and make some money.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Raydar||06-05-2001||09:04 AM||||Remove the distributor cap, and see if the rotor is hitting the terminals inside the cap. If the rotor is not pushed down all the way down on the shaft, that could happen. Would be even worse if the distributor bearings are worn, and allowing the rotor to get a bigger "bite". <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000025||bHooper||06-05-2001||09:39 AM||||will check this evening.  i am also getting the dist. out of a car at the salvage yard... just in case!<P>hoop||||reg||14
